==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact permits two AuditEntry atoms with identical (task, actor, role, op) — a 'replacement' pattern that violates immutability. The injection forces exactly such a pair to exist, so AppendOnly and FR_017_AuditImmutableOutlivesTask both find counterexamples.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditImmutableOutlivesTask
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditImmutableOutlivesTask: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission matrix fact removes all constraints on PermMatrix.Allowed, so the solver can place RelOutsider -> GetTaskById in the allowed set, violating LeastPrivilege and NoInformationLeakage. The injection forces that exact cell to be present.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_ByteEquivalentIsolation, PermissionCompleteness
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalentIsolation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - PermissionCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_ShareeSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ShareeSameTeam.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a user from a different team to appear in taskSharees, violating the cross-team-sharing prohibition. The injection forces a Task whose sharedWith includes a user from a different team.
    expected to FAIL: FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation, FR_012_NoChrossTeamSharing, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NoChrossTeamSharing: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCreatedExists  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditCreatedExists.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Task to exist without any OpCreated audit entry, breaking AuditCompleteness and ValidationBeforeMutation. The injection forces a Task with no Created entry.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_PerEventAuditEntries, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_PerEventAuditEntries: FAIL (expected)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the stored actorRole in an AuditEntry differ from the actor's actual role, producing a misattributed audit record. The injection forces an entry where entryActorRole = RoleMember but the actor's userRole = RoleTeamAdmin.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditAttributionAccurate
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAttributionAccurate: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerInTaskTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OwnerInTaskTeam.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Task whose owner is in a different team than the task's team_id, breaking the denormalization invariant that underpins cross-team isolation queries. The injection forces exactly that mismatch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_009_ImmutableOwnerAndTeam, FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_ImmutableOwnerAndTeam: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

